{
  "model": "medium",
  "language": "en",
  "text": "Mid-course test, track 2. I live in Cairo, in Egypt. Cairo is a very busy city with many people. The River Nile is in Cairo and there are many bridges over the river. But a very famous bridge is the Kasser el-Nil bridge. Cairo has many old buildings and also lots of new buildings. There is a university near the river and many shopping centers, hotels and beautiful parks. At weekends I go with my family to a park next to a big hotel and relax all afternoon. The weather in Cairo is very hot and dry in the summer. And there are sandstorms that come from the desert. In the winter it rains a little but it is still hot. My hometown is in Switzerland. It is small, beautiful and very busy. In the winter we have a lot of snow and it is very cold. But the sky is blue and it is sunny. The summer in the mountains isn't very hot and it rains. But the forests are green. Lots of people come to my town and walk in the mountains or ski in the snow. The town has two hotels, a lot of restaurants and a train station. We also have a supermarket and a park with an old monument in it. Next to the park is a library and there is a little cafe behind it. I go there every Saturday to have coffee.",
